__pycache__/
.vscode
*.pyc
*.pyo
.env
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
node_modules/

# Editor / agent tooling, and the shortcut that points AGENT.md at CLAUDE.md.
# Local to one machine, so it should not travel with the repo.
.claude/
AGENT.md.lnk

# Hand-made backups. The file's own history is in git, so these are only ever
# a local scratch copy.
*.bak

# Local build state: the per-mission metadata catalogs (and the legacy
# combined file they replaced). Regenerated by fetch_sar_data.py; the site
# only ships data/sar_status.js and data/sar_recent.json.
data/catalog_db.json
data/old_catalog_db.json
data/catalog/
# Retired: sar_status.js is now the single full-history file, wrapped so one
# file serves both file:// and the web. Ignored so a stale copy left over from
# an older checkout is never committed back.
data/sar_status.json

# Download lists. fetch_sar_data.py rewrites all five on every run, and
# `git add data/` committed them daily — ~12 MB of churn for files the site
# never requests: app.js builds the .meta4 in the browser (createMeta4) from
# the frames already loaded, so the download buttons work without these.
# Still written to disk, so the size report in update.yml is unaffected.
data/*.meta4
data/meta4/

# Local documentation and tooling. Kept on disk, not shipped to GitHub:
# CLAUDE.md is agent guidance, SETTINGS.txt documents config.js, and serve.py
# is the local http.server wrapper that adds Cache-Control: no-store.
CLAUDE.md
SETTINGS.txt
serve.py

# Local-only notes. Development detail that is not for publication; the repo
# is public, so these stay on disk and never travel with it.
TOOLING_PYTHON_NOTES.md
pwtest/
docs/developer-notes.md

# The forecast mode is deliberately undocumented in public: it exists, and
# only people who already know about it use it. The write-up and the accuracy
# scoreboard it generates therefore stay on disk. forecast_validation.py still
# writes docs/forecast-accuracy.md on every run; read it locally, and re-run
# `python forecast_validation.py` to regenerate it from data/forecast_log.json.
docs/futurama.md
docs/forecast-accuracy.md
